    "description": "•\tDeveloped and maintained batching webtool so the lab could process high volume of Covid samples in an efficient and accurate way.\n•\tImproved systems to handle the increased number of Covid samples from 1000 to up to 6000 samples per day.\n•\tWorked on integration systems to accommodate easy and reliable ways to receive orders and send results for new Covid test facilities.\n•\tWorked on printing and reading 1D and 2D barcodes systems that were provided to our clients to accurately check-in patients and accession samples.\n•\tImproved functionality and performance for data reviewing tools so patients could get results sooner.\n•\tWorked and maintained various clients’ integration systems using a data exchange to support FHIR, HL7, XML and custom messaging formats.\n•\tDesigned and maintained various reports templates in IronPDF, PDFSharp and ReportBuilder.\n•\tCreated various Restful APIs in .Net Core and .Net Framework to support new systems and enhance legacy applications.\n•\tAutomated repetitive manual workflows to automate updating SQL, MySql and MongoDB using transaction scope.\n•\tWorked closely with infrastructure team to migrate network to ensure applications and systems were operational with minimal down-time and impact to clients/users.\n•\tCreated automated builds and releases in Azure DevOps for continuous integration.\n•\tWorked on test first services to maintain reliability.\n•\tMaintained and supported legacy applications in Delphi, ASP.Net webpages and WinForms.\n•\tStandardized versioning across desktop applications to properly identify release.\n•\tMentored Jr. developers to bring them up to speed.\n•\tWorked closely with product owners to refine backlogs, planning and structuring current sprint stories.",
